## Tests and quality

```bash
cmake -S . -B build -DXMPL100_BUILD_TESTS=ON && cmake --build build && ctest --test-dir build
```

The host tests cover every call and every error it can return, with the firmware's flags (`-fno-exceptions
-fno-rtti`, warnings as errors). There is no fuzz target: the library reads no untrusted input. CI also gates
coverage, complexity and sanitizers, and runs clang-tidy, cppcheck and the handbook rules (`.kokeb/handbook.yml`).
See [Testing and CI](docs/testing.md), which lists every gate and its limit.

